Q9. Can a constructor be private? Why?

Interview Ready Answer

Yes.

A constructor can be private.

Purpose

• Prevent object creation from outside the class.
• Used in Singleton Design Pattern.
• Used in Utility Classes.

Example

class Database{

    private Database(){

    }

}

Now,

new Database();

Compilation Error

