Q10. Can we create an object without using new keyword?

Interview Ready Answer

Yes.

Java allows object creation without explicitly writing new.

Ways

1. clone()

Student s2=(Student)s1.clone();

2. Deserialization

readObject()

3. Reflection

Class.forName()

getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance()

4. Factory Methods

Student.create();

Common Frameworks

• Spring
• Hibernate
• JUnit

