Q11. What is Constructor Overloading?

Interview Ready Answer

Constructor overloading means defining multiple constructors in the
same class with different parameter lists.

Purpose

• Initialize object in different ways.

Example

Student(){

}

Student(String name){

}

Student(String name,int age){

}

Java selects the constructor based on parameters passed during
object creation.

======================================================================

Q12. Can a constructor call another constructor
within the same class?

Interview Ready Answer

Yes.

A constructor can call another constructor using

this()

This is called Constructor Chaining.

Example

class Student{

    Student(){

        this("Vishal");
    }

    Student(String name){

        System.out.println(name);
    }
}

Rules

• this() must be first statement.
• Used to avoid duplicate initialization code.

======================================================================

Q13. Difference between this() and super()

Interview Ready Answer

this()

• Calls another constructor of same class.
• Used for constructor chaining.
• Must be first statement.

Example

Student(){

    this("Vishal");
}

------------------------------------------------------------

super()

• Calls parent class constructor.
• Used in inheritance.
• Must be first statement.

Example

Student(){

    super();
}

Important

this() and super() cannot be used together in the same constructor.

